data seed_runner_loudness_split_note: String = "Split out of test.claim.long.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_loudness_witness (witness-cost-class lane, gunbc.roadmap_authority adhoc-0e6f8ea5-158 / adhoc-17a2c30b-7e0, 2026-08-19), on royal-hawk-392's direction during Wave B derivation. The reason is a module-grain actuation hazard, not a content defect: required_floor actuation restores an entire authored module by renaming it out of a long-home prefix, and this module carried seven identities of which only red_seed_runner_failure_detail_projects_located_receipt (moved here, with its seed_runner_loudness_probe_passes / seed_runner_loudness_probe_failure_receipt pair) is a confirmed cost defect — a real, completed, non-censored floor measurement of 75926ms (run 32177951514, [floor-witness-slow] line, BUDGET-REFUSED against the 1552ms ceiling, the witness ran to completion so this is an exact cost, not a right-censored bound), 15x over the 5000ms CPU safety limit. Restoring the seven-identity module whole would have dragged this row back into required_floor discovery alongside the six clean rows Wave B was restoring. THE CAUSE IS UNLOCATED, and that is load-bearing for how this row is read: the parent module's own loudness_witness_note records a THIRD falsified import-closure-pollution narrowing on this exact identity (718 modules/10.1MB -> 62/0.49MB import closure, floor cost unchanged at the same statistical order, 42983-97260ms pre-narrowing vs 75926ms post) — joining two other falsified candidates in the same lane (Class B / rust_test_fixtures_import_closure_witness, and the loop/bind dag_arrow_lambda_witness_test family). An unlocated cause is not a property of the witness's content: the working hypothesis across all three falsifications is a fixed, corpus-wide load/index cost (build_both_closure_edge_index, DESIGN.md's floor-shared-compute-memoization open thread) attributed to whichever claim happens to touch it first, not a defect in what this row asserts. This module is therefore DEFERRED, not disposed: it stays under a long-home prefix (DeclinedLongModule) until the attribution defect is root-caused and fixed at its actual source, tracked as its own lane by royal-hawk-392 rather than folded into Wave B's population."

data seed_runner_loudness_attribution3_note: String = "RELOCATED FROM test.claim.extdeps_scope_placement_gate_loudness_witness's loudness_witness_note (Wave B merge, gunbc.roadmap_authority adhoc-17a2c30b-7e0, 2026-08-19), verbatim, on royal-hawk-392's resolution: this ATTRIBUTION-3 verdict is about red_seed_runner_failure_detail_projects_located_receipt, which the split above (seed_runner_loudness_split_note) already moved into this file before main's #8566 landed the verdict on the file it used to live in. Relocating rather than dropping keeps the finding attached to the identity it is about. NOT re-typed into SharedFillDisposition (#8455) here -- that migration is separately tracked. The phrase 'the same underlying object above' inside the relocated text below refers to loudness_witness_note's third-falsification paragraph on the file this was relocated from, not to anything in this file. DECIDED (ATTRIBUTION-3 lane, dashboard adhoc-68d59f0c-bc2, 2026-08-19): 'the same underlying object' above named a suspect, not a verdict -- this identity was checked directly against the typed shared_fill ledger (#8455), landed after #8457 quarantined this module, so like the sibling witness it was renamed for exactly one CI pass to test.claim.probe_extdeps_scope_placement_gate_loudness_witness (fn body unchanged) on the same throwaway, never-merged probe (#8563, run 32291153434 / job 96192007757), then discarded. Result: this claim appears in ZERO of that run's 17 shared_fill rows, neither as payer nor as consumer. The standard-pool module_path_index/module_graph_facts/reference_edges fills its own entry resolution would touch (the dag+src/v2 and dag-alone keys) are ALL paid_by=<outside-fold> in that run -- pre-warmed during floor preparation before any claim executes, per the documented WARMING precedent in run_required_floor, and so free to every claim including this one. So the shared-fill mechanism is REFUTED as this identity's cost source: there is no first-consumer artifact here to attribute, exclusive or shared. Its ~54-76s cost (this run: 54144ms; run 32177951514: 75926ms) and its RSS growth (this run: +0.96GB, worst single claim; run 32177951514: +1.00GB, also worst) sit entirely outside the shared_fill ledger's instrumented surface -- real per-claim cost, most plausibly still build_both_closure_edge_index (per-MultiEntryIndex-memoized, confirmed never wrapped in the shared_fill API), but this note asserts only what the ledger showed (unattributed), not that unproven mechanism, per the standing denominator-honesty bar."

func seed_runner_loudness_probe_passes() -> Bool {
  false
}

func seed_runner_loudness_probe_failure_receipt() -> String {
  scope_placement_failure_reason(
    exit: scope_placement_membership_verdict(
      observation: AddedPathsObserved { paths: ["dag/extdeps/browser/opera.dag"] }
    )
  )
}

test fn red_seed_runner_failure_detail_projects_located_receipt() -> Bool {
  let detail = seed_runner_bool_false_failure_detail(
    witness: "seed_runner_loudness_probe_passes"
  )
  detail != "returned Bool(false)"
    && string_contains(s: detail, pattern: "returned Bool(false) | ")
    && string_contains(s: detail, pattern: "THIS CHANGE")
    && string_contains(s: detail, pattern: "dag/extdeps/browser/opera.dag")
}
